 "text": "Hi, how have you been? It depends how much you ride. A few hundred miles is good maintenance day between regular washing and inflating the air in the tyres. It' written on side the pump. If it multi stage, use the lowest stage for first use. Then use the higher stages if you pump up from lower tire pressure. Squeezing the tyre between fingers and thumb is quick and intuitive, you'll learn its rough bump and smooth smooth. Go with what the tyre says. If it says lower when wet, follow that. Otherwise, stick with what's on the tyre box.",
